        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "424986",
          "text": "<p>Which one of the following is/are true?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$R \\cap S=(R \\cup S)-[(R-S) \\cup(S-R)]$</li>\n    <li>$R \\cup S=(R \\cap S)-[(R-S) \\cup(S-R)]$</li>\n    <li>$R \\cap S=(R \\cup S)-[(R-S) \\cap(S-R)]$</li>\n    <li>$R \\cap S=(R \\cup S) \\cup(R-S)$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Select",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq10,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,multiple-selects,two-marks",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "424982",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements is $\\textbf{FALSE}$?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$C-(B \\cup A)=(C-B)-A$</li>\n    <li>$A-(C \\cup B)=(A-B)-C$</li>\n    <li>$B-(A \\cup C)=(B-C)-A$</li>\n    <li>$A-(B \\cup C)=(B-C)-A$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq10,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,two-marks",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "424984",
          "text": "<p>Let $A=\\{0,1\\} \\times\\{0,1\\}$ and $B=\\{a, b, c\\}$. Suppose $A$ is listed in lexicographic order based on $0&lt;1$ and $B$ is in alphabetic order. If $A \\times B \\times A$ is listed in lexicographic order, then the next element after $((1,0), c,(1,1))$ is</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$((1,0), a,(0,0))$</li>\n    <li>$((1,1), c,(0,0))$</li>\n    <li>$((1,1), a,(0,0))$</li>\n    <li>$((1,1), a,(1,1))$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq10,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,two-marks",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "424994",
          "text": "<p>If $A$ and $B$ are two sets and $A \\cup B = A \\cap B$ then</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$A=\\phi$</li>\n    <li>$B=\\phi$</li>\n    <li>$A\\neq B$</li>\n    <li>$A=B$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq10,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,one-mark",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "424988",
          "text": "<p>Let $\\mathrm{A}$ be a finite set of size $\\mathrm{n}$. The number of elements in the power set of $A \\times A$ is:</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$2^{n^2}$</li>\n    <li>$\\left(2^n\\right)^2$</li>\n    <li>$\\left(2^2\\right)^n$</li>\n    <li>None of the above</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq10,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,one-mark",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "424985",
          "text": "<p>Let $A$ and $B$ be sets in a finite universal set $U$. Given the following : $|A-B|,|A \\oplus B|,|A|+|B|$, and $|A \\cup B|$ Which of the following is in order of increasing size ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$|A-B|&lt;|A \\oplus B|&lt;|A|+|B|&lt;|A \\cup B|$</li>\n    <li>$|A \\oplus B|&lt;|A-B|&lt;|A \\cup B|&lt;|A|+|B|$</li>\n    <li>$|A \\oplus B|&lt;|A|+|B|&lt;|A-B|&lt;|A \\cup B|$</li>\n    <li>$|A-B|&lt;|A \\oplus B|&lt;|A \\cup B|&lt;|A|+|B|$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "d",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq10,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,two-marks",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "424993",
          "text": "The cardinality of the power set of $A \\cup B$, where $A=\\{2,3,5,7\\}$ and $B=\\{2$, $5,8,9\\}$, is?",
          "type": "Numerical",
          "answer": "64",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.0000",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq10,numerical-answers,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,one-mark",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "424991",
          "text": "<p>What is the Cartesian product of $A=\\{1,2\\}$ and $B=\\{a, b\\}$ ?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$\\{(1, a),(1, b),(2, a),(b, b)\\}$</li>\n    <li>$\\{(1,1),(2,2),(a, a),(b, b)\\}$</li>\n    <li>$\\{(1, a),(2, a),(1, b),(2, b)\\}$</li>\n    <li>$\\{(1,1),(a, a),(2, a),(1, b)\\}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "c",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq10,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,one-mark",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "424990",
          "text": "<p>Let $\\mathcal{P}(A)$ denote the power set of $A$. If $\\mathcal{P}(A) \\subseteq B$ then</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>$2^{|A|} \\leq|B|$</li>\n    <li>$2^{|A|} \\geq|B|$</li>\n    <li>$2|A|&lt;|B|$</li>\n    <li>$2^{|A|} \\geq 2^{|B|}$</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "a",
          "award": 1,
          "penalty": "0.3333",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq10,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,one-mark",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        },
        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "424983",
          "text": "<p>Which of the following statements is $\\textbf{TRUE}$?</p>\n\n<ol style=\"list-style-type:upper-alpha\">\n    <li>For all sets $A, B$, and $C, A-(B-C)=(A-B)-C$.</li>\n    <li>For all sets $A, B$, and $C,(A-B) \\cap(C-B)=(A \\cap C)-B$.</li>\n    <li>For all sets $A, B$, and $C,(A-B) \\cap(C-B)=A-(B \\cup C)$.</li>\n    <li>For all sets $A, B$, and $C$, if $A \\cap C=B \\cap C$ then $A=B$.</li>\n</ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses2026_cs_wq10,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,set-theory&algebra,set-theory,two-marks",
          "category": "Set Theory & Algebra"
        }
      ]
